WEBVTT

00:21.730 --> 00:24.441
An increasing number of youths
are reporting distress

00:24.524 --> 00:27.235
due to excessive expressions of rage
within their peer groups

00:27.318 --> 00:29.904
and the resulting emotional challenges
they now face.

00:29.988 --> 00:32.699
A public servant plagued by
malicious complaints against him

00:32.782 --> 00:35.535
recently took his own life.
According to experts,

00:35.618 --> 00:38.204
a mental disorder called
"intermittent explosive disorder"

00:38.288 --> 00:40.081
is behind this phenomenon.

00:40.165 --> 00:41.624
A recent study found

00:41.708 --> 00:44.419
that academic stress
experienced by our students

00:44.502 --> 00:46.004
is among the highest in the world.

00:46.087 --> 00:48.840
Throughout South Korea, there's
been a slew of unprovoked attacks

00:48.923 --> 00:51.426
and homicides, as well as
a high amount of violent incidents.

00:51.509 --> 00:54.345
A recent study
on the global statistics of suicide rates

00:54.429 --> 00:57.098
shows that,
among all OECD-member countries,

00:57.182 --> 01:00.185
South Korea has
the highest overall suicide rate.

01:02.687 --> 01:03.772
VOLUNTARY ISOLATION

01:04.689 --> 01:05.774
SOCIAL ANXIETY

01:08.485 --> 01:09.819
ROAD RAGE, DATING VIOLENCE

01:21.456 --> 01:23.625
- Hello, sobriety check.
- Yeah, sure.

01:31.716 --> 01:35.095
Officer Lee,
everything good at Domyeong Market?

01:35.595 --> 01:36.888
Yes, everything's fine.

01:47.857 --> 01:49.943
Ow, my neck!

01:52.695 --> 01:55.031
This is just unbelievable.
Were you even watching the road?

01:55.115 --> 01:57.575
For God's sake, you rammed into me,
and I wasn't even moving!

01:57.659 --> 02:00.829
Are you blind or something?
You really gotta watch where you're going!

02:02.247 --> 02:05.667
You can't go around driving like a menace.
Are you listening to me, miss?

02:06.292 --> 02:08.002
- I'm sorry. I'm very sorry.
- Oh God!

02:08.086 --> 02:10.296
Ah, good morning.

02:10.380 --> 02:12.507
Calm down, sir.
Are there any major injuries?

02:12.590 --> 02:15.093
Oh, well, I think I strained my neck.

02:15.176 --> 02:17.137
- Are you all right?
- Yeah, uh-huh.

02:17.220 --> 02:18.555
Okay, here's what you should do.

02:18.638 --> 02:20.431
You can both contact
your insurance companies

02:20.515 --> 02:22.934
to report the accident.
But first, move your cars, huh?

02:23.017 --> 02:24.978
As you can see,
you're holding up a lot of traffic.

02:26.146 --> 02:27.647
Thank you. Bye.

02:31.025 --> 02:31.985
Oh!

02:32.485 --> 02:33.987
Let me help you with that.

02:38.032 --> 02:39.117
NURSE
PARK SO-HYEON

02:39.200 --> 02:40.618
You must be exhausted.

02:40.702 --> 02:41.536
I am, yeah.

02:41.619 --> 02:45.415
I had the night shift yesterday,
so I guess I dozed off on my way home.

02:45.915 --> 02:49.002
You sure you can drive? You might wanna
call a car service if you're too tired.

02:49.085 --> 02:51.337
No, that's okay. I'm awake now, really.

02:51.421 --> 02:52.422
I should be fine.

02:52.505 --> 02:54.966
- Okay. Drive safely.
- Thank you so much.

03:06.186 --> 03:08.688
RANKED SAFEST COUNTRY
FOR 10 CONSECUTIVE YEARS

03:10.565 --> 03:13.026
Look at this. Hey, hey, check this out.

03:13.109 --> 03:14.652
Hey, 5,000 won, man.

03:14.736 --> 03:17.113
- Not interested.
- Only 5,000 won.

03:17.197 --> 03:20.950
You know you want it, don't you?
Just 5,000 won. Just 5,000 won.

03:21.034 --> 03:23.369
Huh? 5,000 won? Come on.

03:23.453 --> 03:26.164
Jeez. Just 5,000 won, huh?

03:26.748 --> 03:27.665
Look, you want it?

03:27.749 --> 03:30.043
Oh my God!

03:30.126 --> 03:31.878
He has a gun! Everybody run!

03:31.961 --> 03:35.006
What? No, no! This is a lighter.
Just a cigarette lighter.

03:35.089 --> 03:36.507
A cigarette lighter.

03:36.591 --> 03:37.967
What the fuck?

03:38.051 --> 03:39.969
Don't you know
that Korea doesn't allow guns?

03:40.053 --> 03:42.847
No one is supposed to own a gun in Korea.
Not at all.

03:42.931 --> 03:45.099
So, you see,
you don't have anything to worry about.

03:45.183 --> 03:46.267
Hey, do you want one?

03:46.351 --> 03:48.311
Huh? Have a good vacation.

03:49.270 --> 03:51.397
Hey, as you can see,
this new gas lighter model

03:51.481 --> 03:54.025
Is realistic enough to fool tourists.

03:54.108 --> 03:55.610
10,000 for an M16.

03:55.693 --> 03:57.487
I'm sure a lot of you
remember those, right?

03:57.570 --> 04:00.615
It's just 5,000 for a Glock.
And they never run out of gas.

04:00.698 --> 04:02.700
Yes, an amazing product. I'm telling you.

04:02.784 --> 04:04.410
THIS SEAT IS FOR PREGNANT WOMEN

04:11.125 --> 04:11.960
Excuse me.

04:13.544 --> 04:15.255
That seat's reserved for pregnant women.

04:16.047 --> 04:17.006
What?

04:18.424 --> 04:21.678
That seat is for pregnant women,
and this lady's just standing here.

04:21.761 --> 04:23.763
- You should give her that seat.
- Oh yeah?

04:23.846 --> 04:26.224
Why the hell do you care, huh?

04:29.602 --> 04:33.314
Well, it's just that, um,
even though the rules aren't mandatory,

04:33.398 --> 04:36.234
the rules were still made
for everyone to follow, so I thought--

04:36.317 --> 04:38.611
Look, man, I'm tired enough as it is.

04:40.113 --> 04:41.322
I'm fine, really.

04:41.823 --> 04:44.075
I don't wanna cause any trouble.

04:49.372 --> 04:52.375
- Look here, sir…
- That's all right. I'm okay.

04:53.126 --> 04:54.919
Besides, I… I'm getting off now.

04:56.546 --> 04:57.505
Thank you.

05:01.134 --> 05:03.636
Just 10,000 won for an M16,
a gun from the good old days!

05:03.720 --> 05:06.472
You see? You won't get a better price.
Here, take a look.

05:11.352 --> 05:12.687
It's so well-made.

05:44.719 --> 05:46.596
How about you watch where you're going?

05:46.679 --> 05:47.764
Okay, I'm sorry.

05:53.603 --> 05:54.520
ENGLISH ACADEMY

05:54.604 --> 05:56.314
Should I look it up?

06:04.822 --> 06:07.825
So what's Party A's perspective?
They should be shocked, right?

06:07.909 --> 06:09.702
So Party A doesn't permit--

06:10.495 --> 06:14.707
Hey. I told you not to barge into my class
if you're going to be late!

06:14.791 --> 06:18.920
Look, everyone, do you see
how terrible he is with time management?

06:19.003 --> 06:22.173
That's why he fails the exam every year!

06:28.888 --> 06:30.181
Get out!

06:49.742 --> 06:51.411
Oh, I feel better now.

07:00.962 --> 07:04.257
These most recent test results are
much worse than the last ones you took.

07:05.550 --> 07:06.801
As time goes on…

07:08.469 --> 07:11.222
this guy and this guy are
constantly at war with each other.

07:11.973 --> 07:15.893
This guy is telling me to do something,
but the other one's holding him at bay.

07:16.644 --> 07:18.062
I find it confusing.

07:18.146 --> 07:21.274
What about… taking your meds
like I told you to?

07:21.357 --> 07:22.400
I get too sleepy.

07:22.984 --> 07:25.445
When I take those meds,
I'm not able to study.

07:27.488 --> 07:29.907
If I fail the exam again,
it'll be my tenth year.

07:30.783 --> 07:33.161
We all struggle with emotions.

07:33.244 --> 07:36.080
Compulsion, anxiety, depression,

07:36.164 --> 07:37.415
things like that.

07:37.999 --> 07:40.585
Except that the ways to control
and alleviate them

07:40.668 --> 07:42.462
might be different for each person.

07:43.379 --> 07:45.548
So am I normal if I have these thoughts?

07:46.340 --> 07:48.801
Only if this guy listens to this guy,

07:50.595 --> 07:52.597
and if you keep them both in control.

07:56.476 --> 08:01.189
Each person has some kind of trigger
that's deep inside their heart.

08:02.773 --> 08:07.695
But a person with a healthy mind
would never pull that trigger.

08:09.447 --> 08:10.823
In your case, Jeong-tae,

08:11.449 --> 08:15.328
your medication will help
to prevent you from pulling that trigger.

08:20.041 --> 08:21.542
Everyone's got a trigger.

08:24.921 --> 08:27.173
Wow, look how many of them came out.

08:27.256 --> 08:30.301
Why is this country
always so rife with conflict?

08:31.302 --> 08:33.221
Wow, look at this crowd.

08:33.304 --> 08:36.265
It almost feels like someone is
inciting the conflict, doesn't it?

08:38.851 --> 08:41.312
You really don't know
how good you've got it, do ya?

08:42.021 --> 08:45.483
Huh? Who cares if someone incited them
or if that's what they really want?

08:47.276 --> 08:49.487
It all adds up to a paycheck for us.

08:49.570 --> 08:51.989
So maybe you should thank them
and take their pictures.

08:52.073 --> 08:55.284
Oh, come on, now, Wang.
You don't really mean that, do you?

08:56.118 --> 08:59.163
Nowadays, all conflict means money.

08:59.247 --> 09:01.707
Hey, you should make
the crowd look bigger in the photos.

09:01.791 --> 09:04.293
Let us rise up to take back our rights!

09:07.088 --> 09:09.549
Because that's
our bread and butter down there.

09:15.179 --> 09:19.267
Open up! It's been ten months
since I've seen any rent from you!

09:19.350 --> 09:21.185
How do you expect me to survive?

09:21.269 --> 09:23.646
You're not coming out? Fine.

09:23.729 --> 09:25.147
I won't stand for this anymore.

09:26.357 --> 09:27.733
Ugh! Oh.

09:27.817 --> 09:28.818
Ugh!

09:28.901 --> 09:30.278
What's that rotten stench?

09:30.361 --> 09:31.237
Ugh!

09:34.073 --> 09:36.742
A pile of unpaid bills and this garbage.

09:37.243 --> 09:40.621
I should have never
rented this place out. This is a--

09:48.045 --> 09:49.547
How does the body look?

09:50.131 --> 09:52.091
There's no evidence
of someone breaking in.

09:52.174 --> 09:54.385
There's no indication
that this is a homicide either.

09:54.468 --> 09:57.263
But given the marks on his neck,
it's most likely a simple suicide.

09:57.930 --> 09:59.140
Okay.

10:00.141 --> 10:01.642
Detective Seo? Detective.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.769
- Yeah?
- I found something over here.

10:04.604 --> 10:05.521
What is it?

10:13.112 --> 10:14.363
What the hell?

10:16.907 --> 10:18.951
- Hello.
- Hey! What are you doing here so early?

10:19.035 --> 10:22.371
- What are they doing here?
- It's okay. Hello, kids.

10:23.289 --> 10:24.582
What are you doing here?

10:24.665 --> 10:26.375
We found this on the street.

10:28.044 --> 10:29.128
Really?

10:31.213 --> 10:33.758
- Hold on a sec.
- Yes?

10:33.841 --> 10:35.551
- Have a lollipop.
- Wow!

10:35.635 --> 10:36.969
- Whoa!
- Thank you.

10:37.053 --> 10:39.055
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey, just take one!

10:39.138 --> 10:42.600
- You can only take one each.
- It's okay. Take two or three each.

10:42.683 --> 10:44.435
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

10:45.102 --> 10:46.062
Hey, Do.

10:46.145 --> 10:48.939
You can't just give away all our candy.
Taxes paid for that.

10:49.023 --> 10:51.108
You've already eaten more
than those kids took, sir.

10:51.192 --> 10:54.070
If my blood sugar drops at my age, pow!
I go into shock.

10:54.153 --> 10:55.655
Does that mean you want one?

10:55.738 --> 10:56.864
I'm not sure.

10:56.947 --> 10:59.408
Although I guess it is
almost lunchtime, isn't it?

10:59.492 --> 11:00.910
Thanks.

11:06.999 --> 11:08.876
- Hey there. What's up?
- Hey, Do.

11:08.959 --> 11:12.421
I'm in a bit of an urgent situation here.
Would you mind dropping by?

11:18.928 --> 11:21.305
- You say you found this on his body?
- Yeah.

11:21.389 --> 11:24.767
In all my years on the force,
I've never seen anything like it.

11:25.935 --> 11:28.771
I called you first because I thought
you might know how to deal with this.

11:28.854 --> 11:32.942
I mean… you're basically an expert
with this stuff, so…

11:34.110 --> 11:35.111
What do you think?

11:38.197 --> 11:40.783
Well, it's obvious
these rounds haven't been reported.

11:41.367 --> 11:43.994
Did you find anything else,
other than the bullets?

11:44.078 --> 11:48.082
No. So do you think
they were smuggled out of a military unit?

11:51.377 --> 11:52.253
I'm not sure.

11:52.336 --> 11:56.424
These particular bullets are only used
by a small percentage of the military,

11:56.507 --> 11:59.009
so it's really hard
to get your hands on them.

12:00.761 --> 12:02.471
What did the deceased do for work?

12:04.014 --> 12:05.182
He was unemployed.

12:06.976 --> 12:08.769
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

12:13.733 --> 12:15.359
He does have a criminal record.

12:15.860 --> 12:18.946
He got released from prison recently.

12:19.029 --> 12:21.907
We checked this whole place,
but we couldn't find anything.

12:24.368 --> 12:25.536
Jeez.

12:25.619 --> 12:28.497
When a single bullet goes missing
in the military, it's a huge deal,

12:28.581 --> 12:31.083
and now we've got
a whole bunch of them. Crazy.

12:35.337 --> 12:36.172
What's up?

12:37.965 --> 12:39.383
Did you find something?

12:49.143 --> 12:50.644
Damn! What is this?

13:05.242 --> 13:07.244
Man, none of these losers have any money.

13:07.328 --> 13:09.205
How come they order all of this crap?

13:09.288 --> 13:10.164
Jeez!

13:17.755 --> 13:20.216
- You're done with this?
- Oh, yeah.

13:44.031 --> 13:45.324
Shut the fuck up, guys.

13:48.202 --> 13:50.079
Would you please just let me study?

13:50.746 --> 13:52.289
So good, babe! Ah!

13:53.165 --> 13:54.333
Ah! Ah!

13:55.793 --> 13:57.127
You like that?

14:07.388 --> 14:09.765
I couldn't make this stuff up if I tried.

14:09.849 --> 14:13.936
Seriously, dozens of bullets
falling out of some guy's ceiling?

14:14.019 --> 14:16.856
If you put that in a movie,
people wouldn't believe it.

14:18.357 --> 14:21.694
But where did a guy like that
even get all those bullets from, huh?

14:22.194 --> 14:24.238
I'm not sure.
Detective Seo's looking into it,

14:24.321 --> 14:25.781
so hopefully he'll find out.

14:26.282 --> 14:29.410
Yeah, wait it out,
and don't get too involved, hmm?

14:29.493 --> 14:32.872
'Cause you're the expert on that stuff,
and they're gonna milk that.

14:32.955 --> 14:35.374
"Ignorance is bliss
and knowledge is a burden."

14:35.457 --> 14:37.251
Isn't that the saying?

14:38.544 --> 14:41.839
So, tell me, you still not gonna take
the next promotion exam?

14:43.215 --> 14:45.634
I like my job.
I'm comfortable enough here.

14:45.718 --> 14:49.889
Yeah, well, I'm uncomfortable watching you
waste your life at the precinct.

14:49.972 --> 14:50.973
I mean, listen,

14:51.682 --> 14:54.852
given your age, your talent,
your experience, and your skills,

14:54.935 --> 14:57.062
you should at least be a sergeant by now.

14:57.146 --> 15:00.816
I mean, everyone else is desperate
to get promoted except for you.

15:01.317 --> 15:02.234
Why? Hmm?

15:02.318 --> 15:06.739
You know, a stubborn police officer's
almost more trouble than…

15:06.822 --> 15:09.950
than my teenage daughter
who's been giving me grief.

15:10.034 --> 15:11.410
What's going on with Se-yeong?

15:11.493 --> 15:13.871
She told me she wants to move out.
How did she put it again?

15:13.954 --> 15:16.832
Something about her work-life balance?

15:16.916 --> 15:19.501
- Don't you think it's time she moved out?
- What?

15:20.669 --> 15:22.713
What, are you taking her side now? Huh?

15:24.256 --> 15:27.301
I mean, she's gonna use up every last bit
of her hard-earned money.

15:27.384 --> 15:28.802
If she wanted to rent a place,

15:28.886 --> 15:30.721
maybe with roommates,
I wouldn't worry so much,

15:30.804 --> 15:34.683
but she wants to take out a loan
from the bank and start a lease.

15:34.767 --> 15:37.353
She wants work-life balance,
I'm always pissed off,

15:37.436 --> 15:39.521
so I'm totally unbalanced all the time.

15:40.564 --> 15:43.317
This way! Do, this is my daughter's car.

15:43.817 --> 15:45.903
- Hey, another round?
- No, we've had plenty tonight.

15:45.986 --> 15:49.698
Sweetie, you can't keep putting yourself
into more debt. Why…

15:49.782 --> 15:51.742
Oh, for crying out loud.

15:52.242 --> 15:53.869
So I hear you'll be moving out.

15:53.953 --> 15:54.828
Mm-hmm.

15:55.329 --> 15:56.455
I'm so excited.

15:57.039 --> 15:59.625
The commute from home
took me two whole hours,

15:59.708 --> 16:03.170
and… now it takes me about 30 minutes,
and the building's totally new!

16:03.253 --> 16:04.088
Isn't that amazing?

16:04.672 --> 16:06.340
Does your place need anything?

16:06.423 --> 16:07.549
Not much.

16:08.300 --> 16:11.553
Well, a sofa,
a TV, and a fridge. That's it!

16:11.637 --> 16:12.638
Get your dad home safe.

16:12.721 --> 16:14.431
Cheapskate. See you!

16:14.515 --> 16:15.891
Okay. Bye.

16:32.074 --> 16:33.325
Come in, Lee Do!

16:33.409 --> 16:35.869
All unit members are isolated.
Everybody, retreat!

16:36.745 --> 16:39.289
We can't! There are still survivors!

16:39.373 --> 16:42.668
We must retreat first.
Retreat now! That's an order!

16:43.460 --> 16:45.170
Sergeant Lee! Look!

16:45.254 --> 16:47.047
Bullets are coming from everywhere!

16:47.131 --> 16:49.174
Help me, Sergeant Lee!

16:49.258 --> 16:50.759
Sergeant Lee!

16:50.843 --> 16:54.013
Whoa! Your grades are really excellent.

16:54.096 --> 16:56.306
And just look at how tall you are!

16:57.057 --> 16:58.851
And you have a black belt in tae kwon do.

16:58.934 --> 17:00.436
I have a degree in PE!

17:00.519 --> 17:02.438
My military service was
in the marine corps, sir!

17:02.521 --> 17:05.983
Ooh!
What an outstanding young man you are.

17:06.066 --> 17:07.192
Thank you very much!

17:07.276 --> 17:09.361
May I, uh, salute you, sir?

17:09.445 --> 17:11.697
Oh yeah, sure.
I'm excited to work with you.

17:13.824 --> 17:16.869
Uh, so then
who will be my training officer?

17:16.952 --> 17:18.871
Uh, your training officer…

17:20.205 --> 17:21.540
Oh, he's right over there.

17:26.962 --> 17:29.715
So, uh, were you
an administrative clerk or something?

17:31.258 --> 17:32.092
What?

17:32.176 --> 17:33.218
Uh…

17:33.719 --> 17:34.887
I saw you earlier,

17:34.970 --> 17:38.390
typing away so diligently and carefully,
I… I just thought…

17:38.474 --> 17:41.810
Being a police officer
involves doing a lot of paperwork.

17:42.394 --> 17:44.938
You'll get used to it, Officer Jeong.

17:45.022 --> 17:48.025
Yeah, but paperwork just isn't…

17:48.108 --> 17:49.860
well, isn't really my thing.

17:50.694 --> 17:54.948
I'm here because it's my mission
to catch every single criminal out there,

17:55.449 --> 17:58.160
and if they're violent,
then I'll just shoot them all.

17:58.243 --> 17:59.745
And then I'll climb up the ranks

17:59.828 --> 18:02.081
and make my way
right into Regional Investigation.

18:02.164 --> 18:05.584
I mean, look at me. I… You know
that's where I'm supposed to be, right?

18:05.667 --> 18:06.502
Yes.

18:06.585 --> 18:08.128
LISTEN TO MY DEAD SON'S MESSAGE!

18:08.212 --> 18:09.922
APOLOGIZE!
BAN DANGEROUS OUTSOURCING

18:30.567 --> 18:31.401
Ma'am.

18:32.820 --> 18:34.446
I'm afraid you can't do that here.

18:34.530 --> 18:37.699
But… I'm not breaking any laws, Officer.

18:37.783 --> 18:42.246
Uh, well, we received a complaint
about you, and so, as per procedure,

18:42.329 --> 18:43.747
we've come to handle this complaint.

18:43.831 --> 18:45.415
- Mrs. Oh.
- Hi.

18:45.499 --> 18:47.709
I'm doing the same thing I do every day.

18:48.418 --> 18:50.003
I'm not allowed to protest today?

18:50.087 --> 18:52.881
It's not that. There's no problem
with single-person protests.

18:52.965 --> 18:54.466
You're within your rights.

18:55.509 --> 18:57.594
There wouldn't be a problem at all,

18:57.678 --> 19:00.764
but if two or more people gather,
then it's reported as a rally.

19:01.306 --> 19:02.558
Do you see that man over there?

19:02.641 --> 19:06.019
If you just step 20 meters away from him,
no one will be able to bother you.

19:06.770 --> 19:09.481
So if someone comes over here,
you know what to do.

19:12.776 --> 19:14.111
SEOBU POLICE STATION
LEE DO

19:15.028 --> 19:16.780
You still have my card, I see.

19:17.322 --> 19:19.283
Oh.

19:20.284 --> 19:21.410
- Excuse me.
- Whoa--

19:22.202 --> 19:24.955
Sir! Sir, wait! Please!

19:25.581 --> 19:27.124
- I just--
- What are you doing?

19:27.207 --> 19:29.459
I just wanna talk for a minute.
Why is that so hard?

19:29.543 --> 19:32.421
- Officer Lee, isn't this favoritism?
- Sir, please!

19:32.504 --> 19:34.256
I just wanna talk to you.

19:34.339 --> 19:36.341
- Please, ma'am.
- In what way?

19:36.425 --> 19:39.511
Doesn't this company report her
every hour for obstructing business?

19:39.595 --> 19:43.432
I mean, shouldn't we, as police officers,
be resolving this as quickly as possible?

19:44.099 --> 19:46.518
Like I said before,
she's within her legal rights.

19:46.602 --> 19:48.270
Please, sir, just for a minute!

19:48.353 --> 19:51.690
Her son signed up to do
dangerous work that no one wanted to do

19:51.773 --> 19:54.443
for a third of
what the permanent employees make,

19:54.526 --> 19:56.278
then he died in a workplace accident.

19:56.361 --> 19:59.489
No one took responsibility
or even apologized for it,

19:59.573 --> 20:01.783
and then they forced her
to cremate his body.

20:03.160 --> 20:06.079
Part of our job is to let people
know what their rights are

20:06.163 --> 20:07.748
and to look after them.

20:08.790 --> 20:11.001
- Why won't you listen?
- Go help her.

20:11.627 --> 20:13.629
- She must be exhausted.
- Jeez, lady.

20:13.712 --> 20:15.297
I just wanted to talk to him.

20:17.174 --> 20:18.050
Ma'am?

20:22.596 --> 20:23.430
Here you go.

20:23.513 --> 20:24.556
Thank you so much.

20:24.640 --> 20:25.515
Yeah.

20:26.266 --> 20:28.185
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

20:31.605 --> 20:33.398
You don't need to keep giving me things.

20:33.482 --> 20:36.860
It's not a problem. If you're gonna fight,
you need to keep your strength up.

20:36.944 --> 20:39.196
It must be exhausting
to stand out here all day.

20:39.279 --> 20:41.240
You should eat something for some energy.

20:41.323 --> 20:42.282
YAKGWA

20:46.161 --> 20:48.914
I don't know how to thank you.
I'm also sorry.

20:48.997 --> 20:51.166
No worries. It's the least I can do.

20:51.917 --> 20:52.793
Okay.

20:52.876 --> 20:55.587
We're standing right in the driveway,
so let's move over here.

20:55.671 --> 20:57.005
- Let me carry this.
- Are you sure?

20:57.089 --> 20:57.965
Yeah.

21:00.133 --> 21:01.760
YEONGSEONG GOSIWON
FULLY FURNISHED

21:21.530 --> 21:22.406
Mm.

21:23.448 --> 21:24.324
Mm.

21:31.123 --> 21:31.957
What?

21:32.916 --> 21:34.209
Someone ate my food again.

21:34.293 --> 21:35.585
What are you going on about now?

21:35.669 --> 21:38.964
My mom sent me a container
of myeolchi jorim recently.

21:39.047 --> 21:41.800
And I wrote my name on it
and put it at the back, hidden away.

21:41.883 --> 21:43.927
When I looked for it just now,
it wasn't there.

21:44.011 --> 21:47.472
Wow. That's awful. Who did that?

21:48.557 --> 21:49.975
I put notes on all my containers,

21:50.058 --> 21:52.853
saying "please don't touch food
that doesn't belong to you."

21:52.936 --> 21:53.979
- Why won't you help--
- Okay!

21:54.062 --> 21:56.481
You're like a broken record,
you know that? Jeez!

21:57.149 --> 21:59.359
You know the guy in Unit 306?

22:00.110 --> 22:01.903
I keep hearing
a woman moaning in his room.

22:02.404 --> 22:05.407
- I think he's sneaking his girlfriend in.
- What, are you serious?!

22:05.490 --> 22:08.910
Why would you keep that to yourself?
I could've been listening to them too!

22:08.994 --> 22:11.246
Outsiders aren't allowed
in the building though.

22:12.748 --> 22:14.499
If a rule's been made,
it should be followed.

22:14.583 --> 22:16.585
So why doesn't anyone follow
the rules around here?

22:16.668 --> 22:18.962
Jeong-tae, listen to me, man.

22:19.713 --> 22:22.299
You can't stay cooped up in your room
all fucking day studying.

22:22.382 --> 22:25.927
Go outside into the sunshine.
Breathe some fresh air once in a while.

22:26.011 --> 22:28.972
You've gotta lighten up.
Stop being so lame.

22:29.056 --> 22:31.600
That's how you get fucked up
and become a social misfit,

22:31.683 --> 22:33.852
like those lunatics
with victim mentalities.

22:34.853 --> 22:35.979
So you're ignoring me?

22:37.439 --> 22:40.317
All the good advice I give you
goes in one ear and out the other.

22:40.400 --> 22:42.694
Whatever, man. I got it.
Go back to your room and study.

22:42.778 --> 22:44.946
Go on. Just go, I got it.

22:53.455 --> 22:55.248
What the fuck are these morons doing?

22:55.332 --> 22:56.750
Fuck this.

22:57.376 --> 22:58.877
Clear. Clear.

23:01.797 --> 23:03.048
Clear.

23:04.091 --> 23:05.008
What?

23:06.093 --> 23:07.511
I'm in Unit 307.

23:09.054 --> 23:11.723
We're not supposed to smoke in the rooms.
It makes it hard to breathe.

23:11.807 --> 23:14.309
That's why the door's open. To air it out.

23:15.685 --> 23:16.937
But if you air out your room,

23:17.020 --> 23:18.855
then the smoke goes into
the rooms around you.

23:19.564 --> 23:21.900
The rule is that this building
is a smoke-free zone.

23:21.983 --> 23:24.611
- And we should all obey the rules.
- You fucking piece of shit.

23:26.363 --> 23:27.406
What's that, now?

23:27.989 --> 23:29.032
The rules?

23:29.699 --> 23:30.909
Hey, you fucker.

23:31.743 --> 23:33.495
Did you write this message?

23:33.578 --> 23:37.541
Do I look like some fucking loser
who steals your nasty fucking food? Huh?

23:39.084 --> 23:40.502
I just put it up so everyone could--

23:40.585 --> 23:41.962
Shut up, you little shit.

23:46.049 --> 23:47.008
Hey, ball sack,

23:47.092 --> 23:49.344
if I see you putting up
another goddamn note,

23:49.428 --> 23:50.679
I'll kill you for real.

23:55.934 --> 23:57.436
PLEASE DO NOT TOUCH
OTHER PEOPLE'S FOOD

23:57.519 --> 23:58.854
Now get the fuck outta here.

24:07.446 --> 24:09.197
Fucking son of a bitch.

24:37.434 --> 24:39.227
Goddamn. Give it a rest, you freak.

24:40.270 --> 24:41.646
Hey, loser. Shut up!

24:44.691 --> 24:46.443
You've gotta keep it together.

24:48.778 --> 24:50.989
Calm down, you maniac!

25:09.716 --> 25:10.884
Control yourself.

25:13.053 --> 25:14.012
Keep calm.

25:59.015 --> 26:00.183
I guess no one's home.

26:02.936 --> 26:03.979
Who's there?

26:05.855 --> 26:07.232
Oh, hello.

26:07.315 --> 26:09.818
Is this Mrs. Park Kyeong-ja's residence?

26:10.318 --> 26:12.320
Park Kyeong-ja… Ah!

26:12.988 --> 26:14.906
Uh, my mom went to get groceries.

26:14.990 --> 26:17.409
Since you installed
a water purifier recently,

26:17.492 --> 26:19.369
this is our first maintenance visit.

26:19.452 --> 26:20.287
Come in.

26:22.622 --> 26:23.957
Thanks for having me.

26:27.002 --> 26:28.003
It's in here.

26:42.475 --> 26:45.186
Have you experienced
any issues with the purifier?

26:46.563 --> 26:47.564
Uh…

26:48.189 --> 26:49.816
No, I really love it.

26:49.899 --> 26:51.192
Totally my type.

26:52.027 --> 26:54.988
Let me know if you'd prefer
a model that dispenses ice.

26:56.781 --> 26:59.117
I can get a special deal on one for you.

27:06.583 --> 27:08.126
Special deal?

27:23.141 --> 27:24.601
What kind of special deal?

27:24.684 --> 27:26.728
Oh, you scared me.

27:30.565 --> 27:32.942
Yeah, there are lots of freebies
that come with it.

27:33.026 --> 27:34.486
Ah.

27:34.569 --> 27:35.779
"Freebies."

27:35.862 --> 27:37.322
Ah.

27:40.700 --> 27:42.410
Would you like something to drink?

27:43.536 --> 27:45.205
Oh, no, I'm fine, thanks.

27:45.288 --> 27:46.289
Ah.

28:16.319 --> 28:18.238
So are you married yet?

28:18.321 --> 28:21.574
I am. I've been married
for quite a few years now.

28:22.659 --> 28:23.660
Ah.

28:25.203 --> 28:26.538
A married woman.

28:27.122 --> 28:29.791
Yes. I guess you aren't married yet?

28:30.542 --> 28:33.545
You should find yourself
a good woman and get settled down.

28:33.628 --> 28:34.504
Oh!

28:36.047 --> 28:36.965
Oh…

29:00.822 --> 29:02.407
You don't think it'll happen, right?

29:02.490 --> 29:03.491
What?

29:04.367 --> 29:06.494
I… I… I'm not sure what you mean.

29:07.620 --> 29:09.038
Me getting married.

29:14.335 --> 29:16.421
Ig… ignore what I said. It was dumb.

29:17.005 --> 29:18.590
I'll finish up here quickly.

29:24.262 --> 29:25.388
Take your time.

29:26.389 --> 29:27.766
I'm going out for a smoke.

29:36.941 --> 29:38.234
You leaving?

29:58.880 --> 30:01.341
Mr. Jeon Won-seong, are you here?

30:03.760 --> 30:06.554
- What do you want?
- Hello. We're the police.

30:07.180 --> 30:08.890
We're here to check your ankle monitor.

30:08.973 --> 30:10.975
Uh, we were told
the signal has been quite patchy.

30:11.059 --> 30:12.727
You have a few minutes for us?

30:13.353 --> 30:14.521
No, I don't.

30:14.604 --> 30:16.022
Well, I guess we could…

30:16.105 --> 30:19.609
Uh, I'm done
changing your water purifier, sir.

30:19.692 --> 30:21.861
- Have a good day.
- Ms. Ko Ji-yeong.

30:23.238 --> 30:24.239
Come back soon.

30:25.281 --> 30:28.034
Next time, I'll switch it
for one that makes ice.

30:40.755 --> 30:42.674
Take a quick look around inside.

30:42.757 --> 30:43.633
Yes, sir.

30:54.394 --> 30:55.270
Oh, my God.

31:00.441 --> 31:01.651
Are you okay?

31:01.734 --> 31:04.153
Thank you so much for coming in just then.

31:04.654 --> 31:06.072
Did something happen in there?

31:06.155 --> 31:08.283
I saw that he was wearing
an ankle monitor,

31:09.784 --> 31:11.369
and I suddenly got scared.

31:11.953 --> 31:13.621
Next time you make a home visit,

31:13.705 --> 31:15.665
you should check
the sex offender registry.

31:15.748 --> 31:17.000
That should help a lot.

31:22.338 --> 31:23.756
Officer Lee.

31:23.840 --> 31:25.300
I'll check his ankle monitor.

31:25.967 --> 31:27.969
I'm gonna check around
the perimeter for a bit.

31:43.902 --> 31:46.529
Mr. Jeon Won-seong,
do you have any family?

31:46.613 --> 31:48.156
I live alone. Why?

31:48.740 --> 31:50.450
You gonna send me a woman or what?

31:53.912 --> 31:54.746
Hmm.

31:55.705 --> 31:57.415
Then who's this Park Kyeong-ja?

31:59.751 --> 32:01.044
She's my mother. Why?

32:01.753 --> 32:03.630
Well, you just said you live alone.

32:03.713 --> 32:07.050
Hey, are you trying to pick a fight
with me or something?

32:07.133 --> 32:08.134
Trying to be funny?

32:09.594 --> 32:12.805
You think I can live a full life under
my own name with this fucking thing on?

32:12.889 --> 32:15.224
For fuck's sakes, man! Seriously!

32:15.308 --> 32:16.476
Oh, you startled me.

32:18.853 --> 32:21.064
Oh, come on.
Look, there's no need to get so upset.

32:25.693 --> 32:27.153
- Whoa.
- You son of a bitch.

32:27.236 --> 32:29.530
You sure do like to
run your fucking mouth.

32:32.158 --> 32:33.785
Please, don't swear like that.

32:34.452 --> 32:36.913
Well, I just did, you stupid motherfucker.

32:36.996 --> 32:39.332
So what're you gonna do? Fucking pig.

32:39.415 --> 32:42.752
All right,
let's just, uh, check your monitor,

32:42.835 --> 32:45.088
then I'll go. Let's see your foot now.

32:46.089 --> 32:48.383
Come on! Show me your foot.

32:49.133 --> 32:50.385
Here's my fucking foot.

32:51.386 --> 32:52.929
Check it out all you like.

33:00.603 --> 33:02.146
So your name's Jang Jeong-u, huh?

33:07.777 --> 33:10.113
Are your parents still alive, Jeong-u?

33:11.364 --> 33:12.448
That's quite enough.

33:21.290 --> 33:22.625
Hi, how's the signal now?

33:23.126 --> 33:24.669
I'm not finding any issues.

33:25.503 --> 33:28.715
I checked the seam and the back of it,
and there are no marks.

33:29.465 --> 33:30.383
Yes.

33:31.551 --> 33:32.719
I feel sorry for you.

33:38.433 --> 33:39.767
You'll be mourned by your parents.

33:46.774 --> 33:48.901
Let go of me! Let go of me!

33:55.450 --> 33:56.701
Any issues?

33:57.452 --> 33:58.411
Uh,

33:59.078 --> 33:59.996
no.

34:00.538 --> 34:02.457
No issues. Uh, the monitor's fine.

34:02.540 --> 34:05.334
Fucking shit!

34:05.918 --> 34:09.172
Why is everyone out to get me?!

34:10.798 --> 34:11.674
Let's go.

34:14.719 --> 34:15.553
Hey!

34:16.054 --> 34:17.221
Stop right there!

34:18.765 --> 34:20.308
I may have committed a crime,

34:20.933 --> 34:23.936
but I've got human rights too.
I've got human rights!

34:25.021 --> 34:27.398
You police are always
trying to mess up my life!

34:27.482 --> 34:29.150
Why?

34:30.485 --> 34:33.488
If you keep watching me like this
and ignoring my rights,

34:34.072 --> 34:35.740
I'm not gonna stand for it.

34:41.162 --> 34:44.707
It's because we respect your human rights
that you're wearing that monitor.

34:47.668 --> 34:48.544
Get it?

34:57.470 --> 34:59.639
Respect, my ass!

34:59.722 --> 35:00.723
Fuckers!

35:01.933 --> 35:04.185
Respect?! Bullshit!

35:13.069 --> 35:14.487
I'm sorry, Officer Lee.

35:17.406 --> 35:19.700
No need to apologize,
but while you're out in the field,

35:19.784 --> 35:20.701
remember this.

35:21.536 --> 35:23.663
Treat complainants and victims
with compassion,

35:24.288 --> 35:26.374
and treat criminals with the rule of law.

35:26.457 --> 35:27.792
Yes, sir.

35:27.875 --> 35:30.837
Uh, I promise I won't forget
what you told me today, sir.

35:32.130 --> 35:32.964
You know what?

35:33.798 --> 35:36.092
- What?
- I can make sure that you don't forget it.

35:36.175 --> 35:37.969
Once we're back, you'll type a report.

35:38.052 --> 35:39.679
In Malgun Gothic, font size 11.

35:40.179 --> 35:41.389
Okay, got it.

35:42.056 --> 35:43.474
I'll type carefully.

35:47.395 --> 35:49.730
Yet another shooting
has occurred in the United States.

35:49.814 --> 35:52.108
At least 15 people were killed
in a shooting…

35:52.191 --> 35:54.485
Man, the US is supposed
to be a developed country.

35:54.569 --> 35:57.446
Why do people get shot there all the time?
It's so terrifying.

35:57.530 --> 35:59.907
Yeah. It's crazy.

35:59.991 --> 36:02.743
But I guess that's why
our country's such a great place.

36:06.372 --> 36:07.248
Don't exaggerate.

36:07.331 --> 36:09.333
But at least we don't have guns
in Hell Joseon.

36:09.417 --> 36:10.293
Strange.

36:10.376 --> 36:12.128
I mean,
we all know how to shoot guns already.

36:12.211 --> 36:13.754
We've all done our military service.

36:13.838 --> 36:17.175
Hey, stop running your mouth
about unrealistic shit.

36:17.258 --> 36:19.468
Oh damn, Bitcoin's down again.

36:19.552 --> 36:22.221
Shit, are you still investing
in Bitcoin? That's an addiction.

36:22.305 --> 36:25.057
No, I got the biggest line
of credit I could manage.

36:25.558 --> 36:29.020
Hey, look. If he wants to
throw away his money, let him.

36:29.103 --> 36:30.229
You'll see!

36:30.771 --> 36:33.399
- I'll call you when I'm filthy rich.
- Whatever, dude!

36:33.482 --> 36:36.194
I've always admired people
who act first and think later,

36:36.277 --> 36:37.737
but now I'm not so sure.

36:37.820 --> 36:40.281
You're full of shit.
You know you are. Let me tell you--

36:40.364 --> 36:41.240
What?!

36:41.324 --> 36:43.284
Authorities investigating the attack…

36:43.367 --> 36:44.827
NO DRINKING! NO SMOKING! NO SHOUTING!

36:44.911 --> 36:46.704
…and are considering additional security

36:46.787 --> 36:49.123
to ensure that the school
and community remain safe.

36:49.749 --> 36:52.210
Whoa. What the hell is up with him today?

36:53.836 --> 36:55.963
One blank round,
five live rounds, all clear.

36:57.757 --> 36:59.717
So can I trust you with that? Hmm?

36:59.800 --> 37:00.801
Sir,

37:01.761 --> 37:05.014
I was the only student
in my entire police academy cohort

37:05.097 --> 37:07.058
who scored with perfect marksmanship.

37:07.141 --> 37:09.060
Yeah, I know, kid. Fill that out.

37:16.817 --> 37:20.112
And what about Officer Lee?
He's not taking a gun with him?

37:20.196 --> 37:21.072
Mmm.

37:21.155 --> 37:23.282
No, Officer Lee prefers his Taser.

37:23.366 --> 37:24.784
Oh, really?

37:24.867 --> 37:27.536
And anyway,
I doubt you'll even end up shooting it.

37:27.620 --> 37:30.373
- But take good care of it anyway, okay?
- Yes, I will.

37:30.456 --> 37:31.916
- Off you go.
- Hmm.

37:35.586 --> 37:36.754
Hmm.

37:40.216 --> 37:41.926
Ah, so nice and peaceful.

37:42.885 --> 37:46.639
- Night duty is gonna be quite simple--
- Get over here, kid! Get over here now.

37:46.722 --> 37:48.015
What the hell was that? Peaceful?

37:48.099 --> 37:50.268
Don't you know that word's
forbidden in a police station?

37:50.351 --> 37:51.978
- I take it back. I'm sorry!
- Never say it!

37:52.061 --> 37:55.147
Jesus, what am I gonna do with you?
You little… Hey, Do!

37:55.231 --> 37:57.316
- Sir?
- Have you even trained this guy? Huh?

37:57.400 --> 37:59.068
For God's sake…

37:59.151 --> 38:00.111
Officer Jeong?

38:38.858 --> 38:39.942
Just shut up.

38:46.073 --> 38:47.158
Oh, come on.

39:01.505 --> 39:04.800
Shut up, for fuck's sake!
I'm right next door!

39:04.884 --> 39:05.801
What the hell?

39:05.885 --> 39:09.472
- Babe, you said no one lived next door.
- So what? Isn't it more exciting?

39:10.806 --> 39:11.640
Look.

39:12.892 --> 39:14.435
Just be a little more considerate.

39:14.518 --> 39:16.437
Oh, fuck off, you asshole!

39:17.188 --> 39:19.231
Or you feel horny too, you pervert?

39:19.315 --> 39:21.359
Why don't you just jack off
while we're doing it?

39:21.442 --> 39:24.904
Listen to me when I'm talking to you,
you stupid sons of bitches.

39:31.494 --> 39:33.454
Why does life have to be so difficult?

39:39.668 --> 39:41.962
This is 112. What's your emergency?

39:42.046 --> 39:42.880
Gun…

39:43.381 --> 39:44.632
Someone has a gun.

39:44.715 --> 39:45.591
Excuse me?

39:48.594 --> 39:49.595
Hello?

39:50.137 --> 39:52.348
I just heard a gunshot.
Where are you located?

39:52.431 --> 39:55.643
- Officer, please! Hurry!
- Did you call the police?

39:59.438 --> 40:02.691
I just asked you
if you called the police or not.

40:02.775 --> 40:04.610
Hmm? Answer me! Huh?

40:04.693 --> 40:07.154
You ignore me,
but then you called the cops on me?

40:07.238 --> 40:09.323
Huh? Come on.

40:11.909 --> 40:14.078
I'm sorry, did you say you heard gunshots?

40:15.037 --> 40:16.038
Hello?

40:17.248 --> 40:18.374
Are you there?

40:21.168 --> 40:22.920
Ignoring me to the bitter end, huh?

40:28.300 --> 40:29.468
I'm the one who called.

40:29.552 --> 40:30.845
And who are you, sir?

40:31.929 --> 40:33.722
- Oh, no, don't call me sir.
- Okay.

40:34.515 --> 40:36.183
I'm studying for the civil service exam.

40:36.267 --> 40:37.601
- Grade Nine, revenue officer.
- Sir?

40:37.685 --> 40:39.520
- The Grade Seven exam was too hard.
- Sir?

40:39.603 --> 40:42.398
Uh, I was gonna call you guys soon anyway.

40:42.898 --> 40:46.068
But these jerks,
they just keep ignoring what I tell them.

40:46.152 --> 40:47.278
Where are you located?

40:47.361 --> 40:49.321
- I'm at Yeongseong Gosiwon.
- Myeongseong?

40:49.405 --> 40:50.239
Yeong.

40:50.322 --> 40:51.407
- Yeong.
- Uh, yeah. Seong.

40:51.490 --> 40:53.325
- Seong.
- On the third floor of Tomorrow Karaoke.

40:53.409 --> 40:55.244
At the intersection next to the overpass.

40:55.786 --> 40:57.746
But there's no point in you coming now.

41:01.083 --> 41:03.043
'Cause I've already pulled the trigger.

41:06.964 --> 41:10.217
How many times did I tell you to go
to the motel if you were gonna fuck?

41:11.093 --> 41:12.678
There's no soundproofing here.

41:18.476 --> 41:19.810
Please don't kill me.

41:21.103 --> 41:22.605
Please don't do it!

41:24.148 --> 41:27.067
